 foreign key     &lt;b&gt;UK&lt;/b&gt;  unique key&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Solid line&lt;/b&gt; — relationship enforced by a database foreign key (&lt;i&gt;ON DELETE CASCADE&lt;/i&gt;). Crow's-foot notation: the single bar reads &quot;exactly one&quot;, the fork reads &quot;zero or many&quot;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Dashed line&lt;/b&gt; — logical reference only; the column exists but no FK constraint is declared (notifications.client_id, personal_access_tokens.tokenable_id, payments.received_by, time_slots.slot_time).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Colour key:&lt;/b&gt;  blue = accounts &amp; identity  ·  green = booking &amp; catalogue  ·  orange = billing &amp; collections  ·  purple = operations &amp; resources  ·  yellow = messaging  ·  grey = framework table.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;equipment&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;manpower&lt;/b&gt; are standalone inventory tables — they are assigned to jobs administratively and hold no foreign keys." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4d4d4d;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="1244" width="1340" height="116" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
